    "created_at": "2026-07-22T21:11:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-22T21:11:17Z",
    "body": "Thank you @ajnart,\n\nI understand your point, and everyone's usage is different, of course.\n\nIn my specific case, left-aligned rows would do the trick. No need for placing a specific item on a virtual point (6,18) on the grid.\nDon't preserve the aspect ratio on width shrink (or at least have a minimum cell size), and when a viewport width shrinks too much - move items that overflow to the next line (so row may have multiple lines in this case).\n\nMaybe another example of a simpler layout (but I have not used it in my environment) for me could be https://demo.dashy.to/ . I also see that it has a bit of an issue at specific breakpoint, but overall it does responsive parts in a reasonable way.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
